Z||000000||penetrator||12-13-1999||01:04 AM||||Ive been talking about my stalling problems before. But now i remeber when it started to stall. It was when after i had changed my gearbox fluid, and droped my Speedogear in to the gear box. So i have't got any speedometer gear yet.(If someone know where to get, my car is a 4-speed manual 86 GT(v6)).<P>Can it be so that the ECM checks with the speedometer or something and when its not "feeling" something from the speedometer, then that can cause the stall ?<BR>Its only stall when it gets warm.<BR>(The engine never stalled before the fluid change???)<P>Regards <BR>Magnus (Sweden)||||reg||1
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||12-13-1999||06:43 PM||||I think it's more a coincidence that the stalling appeared after the change. I'd say it's the ignition module. Maybe you should check that first...||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-13-1999||08:31 PM||||Speedometer pulses are fed to the ECM. Exactly how it's used I do not know. Replace the gear and see if it stops goofing off. That gear should be available at any GM dealer and allot of scrap yards. It's used in the FWD cars to. look around, I'm not sure which cars use it and which use a speedo cable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||12-13-1999||09:30 PM||||AFAIK, the speedometer pulses are only used by the ECM for cruise control and A/C...||||reg||1
